        <h2 id="faq">10. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Does this work for a 40-person onboarding cohort?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              Yes, with a format change. Use a simultaneous-response wheel
              (Wheel 4 above) so everyone answers each spin at once instead of
              waiting for individual turns. For anything needing one-on-one
              answers, split into breakout groups of eight to ten.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Is a digital spin wheel actually random?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              Yes — every spin calls your browser's Web Cryptography API (<code>crypto.getRandomValues()</code>) with rejection sampling before the wheel animation begins, so nobody timing a click can steer the outcome. See
              <a
                href="https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/is-spin-wheel-truly-random"
                >is a digital spin wheel truly random?</a
              >
              for the full technical explanation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            What if someone lands on a question they'd rather not answer?
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              Build a "pass, spin again" entry into the wheel from the start.
              It's a quiet, built-in way out that doesn't single anyone out or
              require an explanation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Does it work for a 1:1 onboarding meeting with a manager?
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              It works particularly well there — it takes the "interview" feel
              out of a manager asking questions one after another. Use Wheel 2
              and have the manager answer their own spins too; that reciprocity
              is what actually builds rapport, more than the questions
              themselves.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Can I make certain questions come up more often?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              Yes — click the <code>+</code> or <code>-</code> weight button beside any question (1x to 20x) to scale its odds without duplicating labels, or toggle duplicate entries if you want separate slices.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Does it work on mobile?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              Yes — spinthewheelsonline.com runs on any device with no install.
              Facilitators usually run it from a laptop and share their screen,
              but it works fine from a phone too.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
